{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"067afb743ff30a20","name":"card_event_rm_roma","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Italy/events/card_event_rm_roma","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"RM ROMA","text":"Deal 4 damage to an enemy. The top card of your deck has the Navy type until the end of your next turn.","flavorText":"The Roma, commissioned in June 1942, was the third and final Littorio-class battleship of Italy's Regia Marina. Equipped with nine 15-inch guns and advanced armor, she was among the most formidable warships of her time. However, Italy's fuel shortages and strategic constraints limited her operational use. On September 9, 1943, following Italy's armistice with the Allies, Roma led a fleet departing La Spezia, intending to surrender at Malta. While navigating near Sardinia, the fleet was attacked by German Dornier Do 217 bombers deploying Fritz X radio-controlled glide bombs. Roma was struck twice: the first bomb caused significant flooding and power loss and the second detonated a forward magazine that resulted in a catastrophic explosion. The ship broke apart and sank, leading to the deaths of 1,393 crew members, including Admiral Carlo Bergamini. Roma's sinking marked the first instance of a battleship destroyed by a precision-guided weapon, signaling a shift in naval warfare. Her wreck was located in 2012 off Sardinia's coast at a depth of approximately 1,000 meters.","faction":"Italy","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["subtype.navy"],"Name":"card_event_rm_roma","title":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_rm_roma_title","SourceString":"RM ROMA","LocalizedString":"RM ROMA"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Italy","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_rm_roma_text","SourceString":"Deal 4 damage to an enemy. The top card of your deck has the Navy type until the end of your next turn.","LocalizedString":"Deal 4 damage to an enemy. The top card of your deck has the Navy type until the end of your next turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_rm_roma_history","SourceString":"The Roma, commissioned in June 1942, was the third and final Littorio-class battleship of Italy's Regia Marina. Equipped with nine 15-inch guns and advanced armor, she was among the most formidable warships of her time. However, Italy's fuel shortages and strategic constraints limited her operational use. On September 9, 1943, following Italy's armistice with the Allies, Roma led a fleet departing La Spezia, intending to surrender at Malta. While navigating near Sardinia, the fleet was attacked by German Dornier Do 217 bombers deploying Fritz X radio-controlled glide bombs. Roma was struck twice: the first bomb caused significant flooding and power loss and the second detonated a forward magazine that resulted in a catastrophic explosion. The ship broke apart and sank, leading to the deaths of 1,393 crew members, including Admiral Carlo Bergamini. Roma's sinking marked the first instance of a battleship destroyed by a precision-guided weapon, signaling a shift in naval warfare. Her wreck was located in 2012 off Sardinia's coast at a depth of approximately 1,000 meters.","LocalizedString":"The Roma, commissioned in June 1942, was the third and final Littorio-class battleship of Italy's Regia Marina. Equipped with nine 15-inch guns and advanced armor, she was among the most formidable warships of her time. However, Italy's fuel shortages and strategic constraints limited her operational use. On September 9, 1943, following Italy's armistice with the Allies, Roma led a fleet departing La Spezia, intending to surrender at Malta. While navigating near Sardinia, the fleet was attacked by German Dornier Do 217 bombers deploying Fritz X radio-controlled glide bombs. Roma was struck twice: the first bomb caused significant flooding and power loss and the second detonated a forward magazine that resulted in a catastrophic explosion. The ship broke apart and sank, leading to the deaths of 1,393 crew members, including Admiral Carlo Bergamini. Roma's sinking marked the first instance of a battleship destroyed by a precision-guided weapon, signaling a shift in naval warfare. Her wreck was located in 2012 off Sardinia's coast at a depth of approximately 1,000 meters."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnAfterDeckChanged","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTurn"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Organic_War_Drums_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Organic_War_Drums_2.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Italy/NavalWarfare/t_rm_roma.t_rm_roma","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Italian WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/RM_ROMA.RM_ROMA","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":279.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_rm_roma_photo","SourceString":"The Italian battleship Roma, circa 1942-43.","LocalizedString":"The Italian battleship Roma, circa 1942-43."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"OnPlayedFromHandVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_OrderAmphibianAssault.BP_OrderAmphibianAssault_C","SubPathString":""},"customName1":"endofturn1","isDirectDamage":true},"variables":[{"name":"affectedCardID","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_rm_roma_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam